tudent Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Online Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Applying for jobs at King's Navigation link Pre-employment checks Navigation link Shortlisting and interview Navigation link Contact recruitment Navigation link Personal information Navigation link How we recruit Quick find Quick find: Internal vs External applicants Deadlines and lead times How we will be communicating with you during the recruitment process Applying for a job at King’s Shortlisting The interview at King’s Pre-employment checks We are delighted you are considering applying for a role at King's College London. We are committed to creating an inclusive and diverse environment to attract and retain top talent. Our recruitment process is designed to select the best candidates for each role while ensuring fairness and compliance. Here is a brief overview of our recruitment process, with links to help you put together your application. Internal vs External applicants Internal applicants are current employees of King’s, including agency-employed workers and students. If the vacancy is marked as ‘internal only’, you will need a King’s ID. Internal applicants should apply through their HR digital services portal , regardless of whether the role is internal or external. You don’t need to register a new account. If you are an internal candidate without access to HR digital services, all internal vacancies can be accessed via the external job board and will be clearly marked as internal. Affiliates and students without access to HR digital services should also apply through the external King’s jobs website. Deadlines and lead times The deadline for applications is 23:59 (London time) on the date specified on the job advert unless otherwise stated. How we will be communicating with you during the recruitment process You’ll receive an email confirming that we have received your application. We’ll also let you know whether or not you’ve been shortlisted for an interview. Please make sure that your contact details, especially your email address are up to date, as we are likely to contact you via email. Applying for a job at King’s For tips to help you put together your application and supporting statement visit our Applying for jobs at King’s page. If you would like to know more about the position before submitting your application, you can arrange a discussion with a member of our staff. Just follow the contact details provided in the job advert for more information. Shortlisting When reviewing your application, we'll assess how well it meets the criteria outlined in the job description. Applicants who best match the criteria will be shortlisted and invited to an interview. We'll let you know the outcome, whether successful or not. Please note: due to the high number of applications, we can only provide feedback to those attending an interview. The interview at King’s For guidance on the interview process at King’s, visit the Shortlisting and interview page for more information. Pre-employment checks If you are interested in working with us, please be aware that we have a responsibility to ensure that all our employees have the legal right to work in the UK. This means that before we can consider you for any role within King’s, we will need to complete some checks to confirm your eligibility. For more information check out our pre-employment checks page. Quick find Quick find: Internal vs External applicants Deadlines and lead times How we will be communicating with you during the recruitment process Applying for a job at King’s Shortlisting The interview at King’s Pre-employment checks Applying for jobs at King's Tips to help you put together your application Shortlisting and interview Applicants who best match the criteria will be shortlisted. Pre-employment checks We conduct pre-employment check before you can start working with us. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social