nu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link King’s benefits We offer a pay and benefits package that attracts the best candidates from around the world. Of course, benefits are about more than pay and time off and we want also to support all our colleagues in looking after their physical and mental health, through inclusive programmes and activities. Benefits of working at King's Work-life Balance – Annual leave is 30 days a year pro rata plus UK public holidays and a closure period between Christmas and New Year (usually 4 days). Where possible, we also operate a hybrid working arrangement and employees can request flexible working from day one of employment. Pension and financial benefits - In addition to competitive salaries, King’s offers generous pension schemes. Staff will also have access to interest-free loans to cover UK visa costs and season tickets, a Cycle2Work scheme and a huge range of discounts on groceries, household items and travel experiences. Family-friendly - We offer enhanced Maternity or Adoption Pay for 20 weeks and Paternity and Partners Pay for six weeks, all from the day you join King’s. We also run a Childcare Subsidy Scheme offering a 20% subsidy for children under three years of age who receive childcare from an Ofsted registered provider. Health and Wellbeing - We offer discounted gym membership and sports facilities, an employee assistance programme, events, free lectures and more. Career Development – we run a comprehensive range of training, for personal and professional development, from online resources and webinars through to structured management and leadership programmes. Community and enrichment – we are building a thriving staff community, from our staff networks to our choir we offer different ways to get involved at King’s. Our Service Time programme also allows three paid days volunteering time, for another organisation or scheme of your choice. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin P