ation Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Equality, diversity & inclusion Navigation link Our culture Quick find Quick find: Our Principles in Action Building a thriving staff community Equality, diversity and inclusion Community & Professional Networks At King’s, the way we get things done is as important to us as what we achieve. Our inclusive and welcoming community embraces a culture with a deep respect for individual differences and collaboration. Our Principles in Action In everything we do, we apply Our Principles in Action: Include – Inclusion is the key to our success. We are committed to treating everyone with dignity, empathy and respect. By reaching out and seeking to understand others, we build the trust needed for a thriving community where everyone can feel a sense of belonging and empowered to succeed. Challenge – We set clear goals and deliver on our commitments, holding ourselves and others accountable for behaviour and performance. We think broadly and look ahead to innovate and drive improvements for our students, staff, local communities, and society as a whole. Support – We invest in our own growth and the development of others, continuously improving by seeking and acting on feedback. We enable others to succeed through effective communication, influence, and leadership. Our decisions are guided by the best available evidence and rigorous inquiry. Connect – We bring together diverse perspectives and expertise to create impact. By collaborating and partnering with others, we share knowledge and promote interdisciplinarity to achieve our goals. We are passionate about Our people are at the heart of King’s strategic ambitions. By supporting our staff to develop their potential within a positive and inclusive culture, we are building a thriving staff community. We are committed to investing in the future of all staff so we can flourish personally and professionally while being respected, valued and challenged to be our best. Inclusion and belonging We pride ourselves on being inclusive and welcoming. We embrace diversity and want everyone to feel they belong and are connected to others in our community. Wellbeing and engagement Balancing professional and personal lives can be tricky. King’s is committed to prioritising the welfare and wellbeing of staff at all times. We aim to create a supportive, healthy and positive working environment where everyone has a good work-life balance and access to support whenever it’s needed. Our hybrid and flexible working policies help colleagues to manage their work alongside commitments outside of work. All staff are invited to join our All Staff Forums, participate in professional and community networks, and give feedback about our facilities and services at King’s. There are lots of ways to get involved in shaping our future. Development and progression We offer a wide range of opportunities for all colleagues to learn new skills and develop in their roles, from individuals who are just beginning their careers through to those moving into management and leadership. Equality, diversity and inclusion King’s is inclusive and welcoming. We embrace diversity and want everyone to bring their whole selves to work and succeed. Our commitment to inclusion means that King’s aims to create an environment where differences are respected, valued, and celebrated. Everyone should be able to bring their whole self to King’s. We recognise the intersections and complexities of individuals’ identities and experiences, acknowledging that multiple factors may affect individuals in our community’s sense of belonging. Our participation in Athena SWAN, the Race Equality Chartermark and the Business Disability Forum self-assessment means we hold ourselves to the highest standards. Find out more about equality, diversity and inclusion at King’s. Community & Professional Networks At King's, communities form an integral part of our staff experience. Joining a staff network is an excellent opportunity to make friends, participate in key decision-making processes, and contribute in shaping our university's strategy development. Find out more about our community networks In addition to community networks, we also offer a variety of professional networks. These networks connect staff members working in similar roles or who share common interests. View previous item “I’ve have been on maternity leave twice and have found the transition back to work really easy because of the support available. I work flexible hours around childcare which has reduced the stress ​​​​​​​of managing work and parenthood.” Aagje Sleightholme, Student Money and Housing Adviser View next item View item 1 View item 2 View item 3 Quick find Quick find: Our Principles in Action Building a thriving staff community Equality, diversity and inclusion Community & Professional Networks Find out more Equality, diversity & inclusion Ensuring equality of opportunity and outcome Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Our culture | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/our-culture Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
