      "description": "Clinical Research Fellow | King's College London Skip to main content Study Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Study Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Undergraduate Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate taught Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate Research Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional Education Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Education & Languages Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Study Abroad Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Foundation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Summer and Winter Programmes Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Accommodation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Mobility Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Visit King's Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding opportunities Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Student Services Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Academic Calendar Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Sport Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Libraries & Collections Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Online Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Clinical Research Fellow Job id: 156486. Salary: (ST4 – ST6) £69,487 - £78,744 including London Allowance. Posted: 27 August 2026. Closing date: 09 September 2026. Business unit: Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine. Department: Department of Inflammation Biology. Contact details: Leonie Taams.  Leonie.taams@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Hospital. Category: Research. Back to job search About us Are you interested in translational rheumatology research? Do you want to better understand and treat pain in inflammatory arthritis? Would you like to be trained by and work with leading rheumatologists, pain biologists and immunologists? We are looking to recruit a clinical fellow to join the Arthritis UK research consortium TOPPIA: Targeting of Peripheral Pain in Inflammatory Arthritis focused on peripheral pain in inflammatory arthritis. The TOPPIA consortium is directed by Prof Leonie Taams and Prof Franziska Denk at King’s College London, and comprises basic and clinician scientists, lived experience partners and policy experts from King’s College London, Guy’s and St Thomas’ NHS Foundation Trust, King’s College Hospital NHS Foundation Trust, University College London, Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children NHS Foundation Trust, Cardiff University, University of Oxford, University of Birmingham, University of Glasgow, and The Rockefeller University in the USA. Together, the TOPPIA consortium will seek to identify new treatment targets for inflammatory arthritis pain, create a biobank of joint samples to study clinical information on pain, improve tailored diagnosis and care and advocate for pain to be prioritised in care and research. About the role We are looking to recruit a Clinical Fellow to study for a PhD degree under the supervision of Prof Leonie Taams at King’s College London and Dr Fran Humby at GSTT as part of a large Arthritis UK research consortium TOPPIA: Targeting of Peripheral Pain in Inflammatory Arthritis aimed at studying the drivers of persistent pain in inflammatory arthritis. You will be responsible for patient recruitment, conduct clinical assessments including pain phenotyping of patients, perform ultrasound-guided synovial tissue biopsies as well as be involved in cutting-edge investigations of synovial tissue samples in the lab. You will also help ensure harmonisation of data and sample collection across the consortium. The clinical aspects of the work will take place in the Rheumatology Department at Guy’s and St Thomas’ NHS Trust (GSTT), which is one of the biggest departments in the country. The laboratory work will be done in the Centre for Inflammation Biology & Cancer Immunology, in close collaboration with the lab of Prof Franziska Denk , on the Guy’s Campus. The successful candidate will need to have a strong track record in rheumatology, demonstrable interest in translational research in inflammatory arthritis, experience in wet-lab or dry-lab research and strong analytical skills. A pro-active attitude, excellent attention to detail, excellent data analysis and record keeping skills as well as strong interpersonal, communication and time management skills are essential. You should be able to communicate and liaise effectively with a wide range of partners and patients. The expectation is that you will work towards a PhD degree as part of your appointment. This is a full-time post (40 hours per week), but part-time working (minimal 80%) could be considered. You will be offered a fixed term contract of 36 months. The fellowship will cover salary, PhD fees (at the UK level), and research expenses. Please note that this post is open only to applicants with UK/Home fee status (usually demonstrated by holding a British passport or settled status) and not requiring ATAS. Research staff at King’s are entitled to at least 10 days per year (pro-rata) for professional development. This entitlement, from the Concordat to Support the Career Development of Researchers , applies to Postdocs, Research Assistants, Research and Teaching Technicians, Teaching Fellows and AEP equivalent up to and including grade 7. Visit the Centre for Research Staff Development for more information. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Full GMC / NMC / other relevant body registration with valid license to practice Applicants should hold a valid UK MBBS (or overseas equivalent), or a 2:1 undergraduate degree in an appropriate subject, or a 2:2 undergraduate degree with a relevant Master’s degree (at merit) and English language requirement: Band D Advanced training in Rheumatology with substantive clinical working experience in the context of the UK NHS Demonstrable interest in and aptitude for clinical and translational research as evidenced by previous research projects, abstracts, posters and/or papers Demonstrable experience in wet-lab or dry-lab research and strong analytical skills A keen interest in understanding the drivers of inflammation and pain in inflammatory arthritis across the life course Excellent problem-solving, record and time-keeping, presentation and communication skills A pro-active and creative mindset with great attention to detail and a strong team player who is also able to work in an independent and self-motivated manner Desirable criteria Training and experience in musculoskeletal ultrasound and/or ultrasound-guided synovial biopsy Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit’ pages. Interviews are likely to be held in late September/early October. This post is subject to Disclosure and Barring Service and Occupational Health clearances. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Clinical Research Fellow | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/156486-clinical-research-fellow Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
