      "description": "Clinical Research Fellow in Adult Congenital Cardiac MRI | King's College London Skip to main content Study Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Study Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Undergraduate Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate taught Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate Research Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional Education Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Education & Languages Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Study Abroad Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Foundation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Summer and Winter Programmes Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Accommodation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Mobility Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Visit King's Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding opportunities Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Student Services Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Academic Calendar Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Sport Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Libraries & Collections Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Online Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Clinical Research Fellow in Adult Congenital Cardiac MRI Job id: 155785. Salary: £38,831 - £73,992 per annum plus £2162 LWA. Posted: 18 August 2026. Closing date: 13 September 2026. Business unit: Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine. Department: Res Dept of Cardiovascular Imaging. Contact details: Kuberan Pushparajah / Ramesh Valapil.  kuberan.pushparajah@kcl.ac.uk / ramesh.valapil@kcl.ac.uk Location: St Thomas Hospital. Category: Research. Back to job search About Us Applications are invited for a clinical research fellow in Cardiac MRI to undertake clinical and research activity focussed on advanced adult congenital cardiovascular magnetic resonance imaging under the supervision of Dr Kuberan Pushparajah and Dr Alessandra Frigiola within the Department of Cardiovascular Imaging, School of Biomedical Engineering & Imaging Sciences, King’s College London. About The Role Applications are invited for a clinical research fellow in Cardiac MRI to undertake clinical and research activity focussed on advanced adult congenital cardiovascular magnetic resonance imaging under the supervision of Dr Kuberan Pushparajah and Dr Alessandra Frigiola within the Department of Cardiovascular Imaging, School of Biomedical Engineering & Imaging Sciences, King’s College London. Applicants should be medically qualified with full GMC registration.  The post is suitable for Specialty Trainees in Cardiology who intend to specialise in adult cardiac imaging sub-specialty or who have already commenced training in general cardiology and wish to gain more sub-specialty experience in Cardiac MRI (CMR), by taking an Out-Of-Programme Experience (OOPE) from their current training programmes.  The ideal candidate would be at the end of their training (Post CCT) and looking for sub-speciality experience in CMR imaging both from congenital heart diseases as well as non-congenital heart diseases perspective to (further) support/expand their medical career or seeking  experience in clinical research. The candidate should have excellent interpersonal, analytical and problem-solving skills with a proven ability to manage projects, work to deadlines and collaborate with clinical teams.  Prior research experience and peer-reviewed publications are highly desirable but not essential. Our Cardiac MRI service is run through extended days during weekdays covering from 08:00 to 20:00 hours, 5 days a week.  You are expected to participate in a rota of shifts across the 5-day working week covering some early shifts and some late shifts.   There will be some requirement to run weekend lists as and where required to help with waiting list pressures. CMR clinical staff may be asked to participate in clinical duties over the festive period and therefore may not be able to take 4 King’s concessionary/closure days at this time. Instead, the entitlement would be provided through time off in lieu. This is a full time post (40 Hours per week), and you will be offered  a fixed term contract for 1 year. About You To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria MBBS or equivalent GMC registered Valid ALS Qualification Clinical experience in care of cardiac patients in both in outpatient and inpatient settings Experience of working in a multi-disciplinary environment Proven knowledge of ICH GCP guidelines Good verbal and written communication skills Good computing skills Desirable criteria Post CCT in cardiology or in last six months for the completion of CCT qualification MRCPCH/MRCP or equivalent SCMR Level 1/2 or equivalent experience and knowledge (as outlined in SCMR guidance) Experience in cardiovascular imaging and or MR including attendance at courses Experience of preparing IRAS/REC documentation. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the next page after you click “Apply Now”. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information We pride ourselves on being inclusive and welcoming. We embrace diversity and want everyone to feel that they belong and are connected to others in our community. We are committed to working with our staff and unions on these and other issues, to continue to support our people and to develop a diverse and inclusive culture at King's. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the advert. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit’ pages. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Clinical Research Fellow in Adult Congenital Cardiac MRI | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/155785-clinical-research-fellow-in-adult-congenital-cardiac-mri Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
